📊 Social Media (Meta) SQL Analytics Project

🎉 I’ve successfully completed a Social Media SQL Project, where I worked extensively on analyzing large-scale social media data using SQL to extract meaningful and actionable insights.

🔍 Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing social media platform data using SQL to uncover insights related to user engagement, content performance, hashtag trends, and influencer identification. The goal is to transform raw relational data into meaningful, business-oriented insights that support data-driven decision-making.

🗂 Dataset Description
The analysis is performed on a relational database containing the following tables:
users – User profile information
photos – Posts created by users
likes – Likes on posts
comments – Comments on posts
follows – Follower–following relationships
tags – Hashtag metadata
photo_tags – Mapping between photos and hashtags

🎯 Objectives
Analyze user engagement across posts, likes, and comments
Identify high-performing content and trending hashtags
Segment users based on engagement behavior
Detect potential influencers using reach and engagement metrics
Generate actionable insights for content and marketing strategies

📌 Key Insights
Identified peak engagement hours to optimize posting schedules
Certain hashtags and content themes consistently drive higher engagement
Users with high engagement per post and diverse hashtag usage are strong influencer candidates
Tag diversity improves content discoverability and sustained engagement
Users can be segmented into active, moderate, and inactive groups for targeted strategies

🧠 SQL Concepts Used
JOINs (INNER, LEFT)
Aggregation functions (COUNT, SUM, AVG)
Window functions (RANK)
Common Table Expressions (CTEs)
Subqueries
Data quality checks (NULL & duplicate handling)

📈 Business Use Cases
Content optimization and posting strategy
Hashtag recommendation systems
Influencer identification for marketing campaigns
User segmentation for personalized targeting
Re-engagement strategies for inactive users

🛠 Tools & Technologies
SQL (MySQL)
Relational Database Analysis
Data Analytics & Reporting

🚀 Conclusion
This project demonstrates how SQL can be used to analyze complex social media data and extract insights that directly support business and marketing decisions. It highlights the power of structured querying in transforming raw data into strategic intelligence.
